---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Research Methodology — Better Pila"
  description="How Better Pila discovers, verifies, summarizes, and maintains public municipal information in Pila, Laguna."
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="narrow">
      <div class="breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span class="breadcrumb-sep">/</span>
        <span>Methodology</span>
      </div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Evidence Before Publication</p>
      <h1>How records earn their place here.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        We adhere to a strict editorial methodology designed to minimize bias, eliminate unverified claims, and provide transparent civic data.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section narrow">
    <article class="paper content">
      <div style="display: grid; gap: 1.8rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <!-- Pillar 1 -->
        <div style="border-left: 4px solid var(--navy-2); padding-left: 1.4rem;">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">
            <span class="docket-chip" style="color: var(--gold-dark); background: var(--gold-soft); border-color: var(--gold-border);">Protocol 01</span>
            <h2 style="margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 1.3rem; color: var(--navy-deep);">Primary Government Sources First</h2>
          </div>
          <p style="margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.65;">
            We index information derived directly from primary public records: certified municipal ordinances signed by the Sangguniang Bayan, executive orders issued by the Municipal Mayor, Commission on Audit (COA) Annual Audit Reports, and official DILG Full Disclosure submissions. Secondary news articles or social media reports are treated solely as discovery leads—never as conclusive evidence for factual claims.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Pillar 2 -->
        <div style="border-left: 4px solid var(--navy-2); padding-left: 1.4rem;">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">
            <span class="docket-chip" style="color: var(--gold-dark); background: var(--gold-soft); border-color: var(--gold-border);">Protocol 02</span>
            <h2 style="margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 1.3rem; color: var(--navy-deep);">Mandatory Human Review & Dual-Key Verification</h2>
          </div>
          <p style="margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.65;">
            Every record requires explicit human verification, primary source attachment, and review prior to publication. Numerical amounts, official titles, effective dates, and statutory references are checked against primary document scans. Unreviewed entries remain strictly sequestered in quarantine.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Pillar 3 -->
        <div style="border-left: 4px solid var(--navy-2); padding-left: 1.4rem;">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">
            <span class="docket-chip" style="color: var(--gold-dark); background: var(--gold-soft); border-color: var(--gold-border);">Protocol 03</span>
            <h2 style="margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 1.3rem; color: var(--navy-deep);">Explicit Acknowledgment of Gaps & Limitations</h2>
          </div>
          <p style="margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.65;">
            When official documentation is incomplete, illegible, or conflicting, Better Pila explicitly documents the gap rather than extrapolating or making editorial assumptions. A missing budget item is never assumed to be zero without official certified certification.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Pillar 4 -->
        <div style="border-left: 4px solid var(--navy-2); padding-left: 1.4rem;">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">
            <span class="docket-chip" style="color: var(--gold-dark); background: var(--gold-soft); border-color: var(--gold-border);">Protocol 04</span>
            <h2 style="margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 1.3rem; color: var(--navy-deep);">Scheduled Recertification Audits</h2>
          </div>
          <p style="margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.65;">
            Municipal contacts, office assignments, capital projects, and leadership roles are scheduled for regular periodic audits to prevent information decay. Historical legislation is retained with clear status markers indicating whether an ordinance remains active or has been amended/superseded.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Pillar 5 -->
        <div style="border-left: 4px solid var(--navy-2); padding-left: 1.4rem;">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">
            <span class="docket-chip" style="color: var(--gold-dark); background: var(--gold-soft); border-color: var(--gold-border);">Protocol 05</span>
            <h2 style="margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 1.3rem; color: var(--navy-deep);">Public Corrections Ledger & Evidentiary Standard</h2>
          </div>
          <p style="margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.65;">
            We invite residents, barangay officials, and municipal staff to submit corrections accompanied by primary documentation. When corrections are verified, changes are logged transparently to ensure an uncompromised public record.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-top: 2.2rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem;">
        <span style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--ink-soft);">Have an official municipal document to submit?</span>
        <a href="/corrections" class="button button-primary">Submit primary document →</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
